#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exp_integral_ei

#% text
# `exp_integral_ei(x)` gives the exponential integral `Ei(x)`, the principal value of the integral of `exp(t)/t` for `t` from `-inf` to `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 6.2.5. `Ei` has a logarithmic singularity at 0 and is negative for `x < 0`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values; exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# `exp_integral_ei` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exp_integral_ei(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.8951178163559368

#% cell
exp_integral_ei(-1.0)
#% output
#= -0.21938393439552029

#% cell
n(exp_integral_ei(2), 30)
#% output
#= 4.954234356001890163379505130227035

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Large arguments:

#% cell
exp_integral_ei(50.0)
#% output
#= 1.058563689713169e20

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
exp_integral_ei(1.0 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 1.7646259855638542 + 2.3877698515105226im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(exp_integral_ei(x), x)
#% output
#= exp(x)/x

#% text
# The logarithmic integral is `Ei` of a logarithm:

#% cell
log_integral(10.0) - exp_integral_ei(log(10.0))
#% output
#= -8.881784197001252e-16

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp_integral_e`, `log_integral`, `sin_integral`, `cos_integral`
